  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, the skewness of the lotteries — is not addressed in the verbal report. The individual does not mention the concept of skewness, nor do they compare the distribution of probabilities around the mean or note that a greater portion of probability is assigned to favorable outcomes in A. Instead, the justification centers on the perceived higher chance of winning more money and the rarity of loss, which reflects a different reasoning (e.g., risk preference or optimism). Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. While the outcome of choosing Lottery A coincidentally aligns with the skewness reason, the reasoning process described does not reflect the application of the skewness rule. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
