  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual does not evaluate the probability distribution across outcomes or compare the skewness of the lotteries. Instead, the individual focuses on the absolute value of the prize and the similarity of probabilities, reasoning that a higher prize with similar chances leads to a better chance to win more. This justification does not align with the rule of the decision reason, which requires assessing the skewness (i.e., the proportion of probability on favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes) and preferring the more left-skewed lottery. Since the individual neither identifies nor applies the skewness criterion, the decision reason was not used. Therefore, the assessment is that the decision reason was not used.",
